A||||7||Gokart||I'M BACK!! RUNNING AWESOME!!
Z||000000||Gokart||07-22-99||07:13 PM||||Hey Chadman and Batboy thanks for having me get in touch with Ed Parks! He was curious about the dealer telling me that 1,3 and 5 cylinders were very low in compression so he had me check something so obvious, the fuses! Their are two fuses I didn't know that run each bank of the engine. Well this morning after checking both they looked fine and I went back into my depression. I changed them anyway and took a ride, no difference. Then I figured I'd take one out at a time while I was driving and see if that would make a difference. As soon as I pulled the fuse block down to remove one, I got all my POWER back!! Good thing there wasn't anyone in front of me! Their must be a loose wire somewhere behind the fuse block! Much easier fix than replacing the engine like the dealer told me I have to. I thought taking my Fiero there would show how much I really love this car, but they know and are as smart as any other mechanic. After that scare it made me realize-I better put some cash away so I'll be ready when the inevitable does come! Can't bear the thought of driving anything else!! Thanks again guys.
Z||000001||Cooter||07-22-99||07:32 PM||||Wow! Great news. I believe that I would go back to the dealership and have some words with the service manager and the idiot mechanic who came up with the low compression theory.
Z||000002||Gokart||07-22-99||07:42 PM||||Can't say on line what I'd really like to do to that place. Let's just say maybe some made appointments then no shows will do. 
Z||000003||batboy||07-22-99||08:36 PM||||I'd run another compression check, obviously don't let that dealership do it. You might still have marginal compression in those cylinders, but the main problem was that fuse box loose connection problem. If the second compression check shows nothing wrong, then I'd go to that dealer and camp out there bitching at everyone all the way up their chain of command to the big boss until I got my money back. Threaten to turn them into the attorney general for attempted fraud and mention law suit or something like that to get their attention.
Z||000004||ChadMan||07-23-99||08:10 AM||||That is fantastic, Gokart!  Glad you're rolling again.<p>Ed Parks is the man, isn't he?  Not to disrespect other Fiero gurus out there, but Ed really knows his s**t and seems to work on Fieros not just for the money, but also for the love of the car.  I have been lucky with my Fieros, but when/if they ever need major service (clutch or engine swap), I'll be calling Ed.
